<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Wave 02 "Obscura": the latest drop is a CONTACT SHEET (`edition: "sheet"`, DESIGN §7.5,
      §10.2), and the tile under it is squarer (the owner's decision: "one more row at the bottom for sure, the rest
      of the composition is up to you").

      The sheet is four random frames in justified rows (two by two) under a data line, without
      cropping or rotation. How many grid rows it needs is computed from the column width:
      10 columns = 376px at the 1536 reference, 344 inside the tile; two landscape 3:2 frames in a row give a row of
      112px, two rows with a gap 228, plus a header ~22 and margins 32 gives 282. Eleven rows
      (308px) is the first integer the sheet fits in: ten give 280. 10×11 is noticeably
      squarer than the old 10×9 (1.22 against 1.49). The first attempt, a 3×3 grid of 3:2 cells with
      portrait frames rotated, was dropped by the owner after a live run: busy, and
      flipping photos is undesirable.

      Two rows are taken from the left column's neighbours, one from each: calendar 10→9
      (280→252px; a day cell ~44px, a touch target), stats 7→6 (196→168px). Taking both from one
      would mean either squeezing the calendar to 8 rows (cells below a touch target) or the stats to 5
      (a chart with 108px of inner height). The other columns are untouched: the right and central ones
      live on their own axes.

      The column after the seed: drop 1–11 · calendar 13–21 · stats 23–28 (spacers 12 and 22).
    -->
    <changeSet id="0600-wave-02-drop-sheet" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,latestDrop}', $J${"col": 5, "row": 1, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 11, "edition": "sheet"}$J$::jsonb),
            '{tiles,calendar}',
            $J${"col": 5, "row": 13, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 9}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{tiles,stats}',
        $J${"col": 5, "row": 23, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 6}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,latestDrop}', $J${"col": 5, "row": 1, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 9}$J$::jsonb),
            '{tiles,calendar}',
            $J${"col": 5, "row": 11, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 10}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{tiles,stats}',
        $J${"col": 5, "row": 22, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 7}$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-02';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
